cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository (code, materials, or data), please cite it. If you
  refer to the study itself, please cite the preprint under `preferred-citation`.
title: >-
  Reification Gradient: Authority-Gated Reification of a Fabricated Diagnostic
  Category in LLMs
abstract: >-
  A controlled, synthetic-only test of the diagnostician half of Hacking's
  looping effect in large language models. Holding a fabricated diagnostic
  category's descriptive content constant and minimal, the study varies only the
  authority (legitimacy level, L1-L5) of the source describing it and measures
  whether the model fabricates and reifies clinical structure it was never given.
  Design: 4 disorder types x 5 legitimacy levels x 2 open-weight model families,
  preregistered (tag prereg-v1) before the confirmatory run.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Antonio
    family-names: Bernal Suárez
    email: bernalsuarezantonio@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/bernalsuarezantonio-bit/reification-gradient'
license:
